1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,575
This matrix eats three

2
00:00:01,575 --> 00:00:03,750
numbers and returns two.

3
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:05,775
Some inputs vanish completely.

4
00:00:05,775 --> 00:00:07,287
Which ones, and how many?

5
00:00:07,867 --> 00:00:09,079
Subtract twice row one

6
00:00:09,079 --> 00:00:11,729
from row two: all zeros.

7
00:00:11,729 --> 00:00:13,954
One pivot, so the rank is one.

8
00:00:14,567 --> 00:00:17,355
Two special solutions, minus two,

9
00:00:17,355 --> 00:00:19,742
one, zero and minus two, zero,

10
00:00:19,742 --> 00:00:21,279
one, both go to zero.

11
00:00:21,867 --> 00:00:23,580
So does every mix of them:

12
00:00:23,967 --> 00:00:26,167
a whole plane, the nullspace,

13
00:00:26,167 --> 00:00:28,392
of dimension three minus one,

14
00:00:28,392 --> 00:00:29,229
which is two.

15
00:00:29,833 --> 00:00:32,021
The row, one, two, two,

16
00:00:32,021 --> 00:00:34,008
has zero dot product with both,

17
00:00:34,008 --> 00:00:35,246
so the row space stands

18
00:00:35,246 --> 00:00:36,658
perpendicular to that plane.

19
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:39,733
Take x equals minus one, three,

20
00:00:39,733 --> 00:00:40,458
two.

21
00:00:40,458 --> 00:00:41,571
It is the row plus

22
00:00:41,571 --> 00:00:43,196
the first special solution.

23
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:44,825
Apply A.

24
00:00:44,825 --> 00:00:45,850
The nullspace part is

25
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:47,363
crushed to zero,

26
00:00:47,363 --> 00:00:49,163
and the row part lands on nine,

27
00:00:49,163 --> 00:00:50,038
eighteen.

28
00:00:50,038 --> 00:00:51,125
That is A x.

29
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:54,025
Every output is a multiple of one,

30
00:00:54,025 --> 00:00:56,488
two: the column space.

31
00:00:56,488 --> 00:00:59,125
Its perpendicular, through two,

32
00:00:59,125 --> 00:01:01,213
minus one, is never reached.

33
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:02,800
One kept plus two

34
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,400
crushed makes three inputs.

35
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:06,413
One reached plus one

36
00:01:06,413 --> 00:01:08,525
missed makes two outputs.

37
00:01:09,087 --> 00:01:10,100
In general,

38
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:12,438
rank r keeps r input directions

39
00:01:12,438 --> 00:01:14,250
and crushes n minus r.
